{
  "_rules": [
    "Matching uses the first 4 letters of the typed word, case and accents ignored (a word shorter than 4 letters only matches itself). Never put a ligature (oe/ae) in a typed word: 'coeur', not the joined form.",
    "TLK dialogues: set keyword1/keyword2 to the French word given by keywords[tlk[k]] (or tlkOverrides for that NPC). The NPC's own texts and every other text that points to that keyword ('ask about the bell') must use that same word, ideally in its exact form, so the player knows what to type.",
    "Per NPC, the 4-letter prefixes of the two keywords differ from each other and from the topic words (adieu, nom, aspect, metier, sante, rejoindre, donner): checked by test-output/check-glossary.cjs.",
    "Never translate the words in 'keep' (mantras, word of passage and its syllables, proper names of people, towns, castles and dungeons).",
    "Thou/thee -> tu/toi; archaic, solemn, concise. The eight virtues: Sincerite (not Honnetete: honesty and honor would share 'honn' in Lord British's and Hawkwind's 4-letter matching), Compassion, Vaillance, Justice, Sacrifice, Honneur, Spiritualite, Humilite. Adjectives: sincere, compatissant, vaillant, juste, sacrificiel/devoue, honorable, spirituel, humble.",
    "Spell names keep the English initial letter (spells are cast by letter) and are at most 10 characters.",
    "A few typed words are shorter than 4 letters because French has nothing natural longer: nom, vie, mal, vin, ca. They match only when typed in full."
  ],
